% Speech Generating Devices: LCD L33739 and its Policy Article A52469 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for a speech generating device (E2500, E2502, E2504, E2506,
% E2508, E2510), speech generating software (E2511), a mounting system
% (E2512), an electromyographic sensor (E2513) or another accessory (E2599)
% is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
%   - a device or software meets the LCD's criteria 1–7: (1) before the
%     delivery, a formal written evaluation of the cognitive and
%     communication abilities by a speech-language pathologist (SLP), with
%     the elements a–f the LCD lists; (2) a medical condition resulting in a
%     severe expressive speech impairment; (3) speaking needs that natural
%     communication methods cannot meet; (4) other forms of treatment
%     considered and ruled out; (5) the impairment will benefit from the
%     device ordered; (6) the SLP's evaluation and recommendation forwarded
%     to the treating practitioner before the device is ordered; (7) an SLP
%     who is not an employee of the supplier and has no financial
%     relationship with it — and the beneficiary has no other device ("claims
%     for more than one SGD will be denied");
%   - an accessory meets the base device's criteria 1–7; an eye tracking
%     (ocular tracking) accessory or the electromyographic sensor (with an
%     E2510 only) needs a demonstrated medical need; an alternative input
%     device or a head control mouse needs a beneficiary unable to use
%     standard input devices; a mounting system, a key guard or a power
%     wheelchair interface needs nothing more. The protective case (not
%     separately payable) and the carrying case (a convenience item, denied
%     as noncovered) have no rule.
% The benefit is durable medical equipment (Policy Article A52469, Social
% Security Act §1861(s)(6)).
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact: the
% date of the SLP's evaluation and the elements it includes (a list, as the
% standard written order's elements in dmepos.le), the date it was forwarded
% to the treating practitioner, the SLP's independence from the supplier,
% another device the beneficiary has, what kind of accessory an E2599 is.
% The criteria that are clinical judgments are the judged template of
% dmepos.le; the findings this policy reads, and the criterion each stands
% for:
%   severe expressive speech impairment (2); natural communication
%   insufficient (3); other treatments ruled out (4); device will benefit
%   speech (5); tracking accessory medically needed (eye tracking, gaze
%   interaction and electromyographic sensor accessories: "a demonstrated
%   medical need"); standard input devices unusable (an alternative input
%   device, a head control mouse).
%
% The payment conditions the Policy Article adds ("Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: for an E2599 accessory,
% its medical necessity documented in the SLP's formal evaluation (for an
% alternative input device: why standard input devices cannot be used); for
% E2511, E2512, E2513 and E2599, the claim states the item's description,
% manufacturer name, product name and number ("the product identification"),
% and for E2599 the supplier's price list amount.
%
% Not modelled: element g of criterion 1 and the upgrades within the five
% year useful lifetime (statutorily noncovered: no rule concludes an
% upgrade); the DME definition of the device (a general computing device is
% coded A9270 and is outside this policy); the KX, GA and GZ modifiers; the
% PDAC coding verification of E2510; the batteries (A4601).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of *a beneficiary* on *a date*; undefined.
    the written evaluation of *a beneficiary* includes *an element*; undefined.
    the written evaluation of *a beneficiary* was forwarded to the treating practitioner on *a date*; undefined.
    the speech language pathologist who evaluated *a beneficiary* has no financial relationship with the supplier; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has another speech generating device; undefined.
    the accessory type of *an item* is *a type*; undefined.
    the written evaluation of *a beneficiary* documents the need for *an item*; undefined.
    *a claim* states the product identification of *an item*; undefined.
    *a claim* states the supplier price list amount of *an item*; undefined.
    % the lists
    *an element* is a required element of the written evaluation.
    % derived
    *an item* is a speech generating device.
    *a beneficiary* meets the speech generating device criteria for *a device*.
    the written evaluation of *a beneficiary* is complete before the delivery of *a device*.
    the written evaluation of *a beneficiary* reached the treating practitioner before the order for *a device*.
    the accessory specific criteria are met for *an item*.
    the accessory documentation is met for *an item*.
    the product identification requirement is met for *a claim*.

the knowledge base speech_generating_devices includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base speech_generating_devices includes:

LCD L33739 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33739".
the text of LCD L33739 is at "sources/lcd/L33739.txt".
Policy Article A52469 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52469".
the text of Policy Article A52469 is at "sources/article/A52469.txt".

% What a speech generating device is, by code.
rule sgd_device with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "A speech generating device (SGD) (E2500, E2502, E2504, E2506, E2508, E2510, E2511) is covered when all of the following criteria (1-7) are met":
an item is a speech generating device
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E2500", "E2502", "E2504", "E2506", "E2508", "E2510", "E2511"].

% The elements the SLP's written evaluation must include (criterion 1, a-f).
current communication impairment is a required element of the written evaluation,
    as stated in LCD L33739, confer "Current communication impairment, including the type, severity, language skills, cognitive ability, and anticipated course of the impairment".
assessment of natural modes of communication is a required element of the written evaluation,
    as stated in LCD L33739, confer "An assessment of whether the individual's daily communication needs could be met using other natural modes of communication".
functional communication goals is a required element of the written evaluation,
    as stated in LCD L33739, confer "A description of the functional communication goals expected to be achieved and treatment options".
rationale for the device selected is a required element of the written evaluation,
    as stated in LCD L33739, confer "Rationale for selection of a specific device and any accessories".
treatment plan with a training schedule is a required element of the written evaluation,
    as stated in LCD L33739, confer "Demonstration that the beneficiary possesses a treatment plan that includes a training schedule for the selected device".
abilities to use the device is a required element of the written evaluation,
    as stated in LCD L33739, confer "The cognitive and physical abilities to effectively use the selected device and any accessories to communicate".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
rule sgd_codes with provenance Policy Article A52469,
        confer "Speech generating devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(6))":
the policy for code a code is speech_generating_devices
    if the code is in ["E2500", "E2502", "E2504", "E2506", "E2508", "E2510", "E2511", "E2512", "E2513", "E2599"].

section applicability is:

rule sgd_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52469,
        confer "Speech generating devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(6))":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is speech_generating_devices.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The device (or the software): criteria 1-7, one device only.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule sgd_covered with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "A speech generating device (SGD) (E2500, E2502, E2504, E2506, E2508, E2510, E2511) is covered when all of the following criteria (1-7) are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a speech generating device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the speech generating device criteria for the item
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary has another speech generating device.

% The passage of the last condition: "Codes E2500, E2502, E2504, E2506,
% E2508, E2510, E2511 perform the same essential function - speech
% generation. Therefore, claims for more than one SGD will be denied as not
% reasonable and necessary."

rule sgd_criteria with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "If one or more of the SGD coverage criteria 1-7 is not met, the SGD will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a beneficiary meets the speech generating device criteria for a device
    if the written evaluation of the beneficiary is complete before the delivery of the device
    and the finding severe expressive speech impairment about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding natural communication insufficient about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding other treatments ruled out about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding device will benefit speech about the beneficiary is established
    and the written evaluation of the beneficiary reached the treating practitioner before the order for the device
    and the speech language pathologist who evaluated the beneficiary has no financial relationship with the supplier.

% Criterion 1: the SLP's formal written evaluation, before the delivery,
% with every required element.
rule sgd_evaluation with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "Prior to the delivery of the SGD, the beneficiary has had a formal evaluation of their cognitive and communication abilities by a speech-language pathologist (SLP)":
the written evaluation of a beneficiary is complete before the delivery of a device
    if the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of the beneficiary on a date
    and the device was delivered on an other date
    and the date is before or equal to the other date
    and for all cases in which
            an element is a required element of the written evaluation
        it is the case that
            the written evaluation of the beneficiary includes the element.

% Criterion 6: the evaluation reached the treating practitioner before the
% order.
rule sgd_forwarded with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "A copy of the SLP's written evaluation and recommendation have been forwarded to the beneficiary's treating practitioner prior to ordering the device":
the written evaluation of a beneficiary reached the treating practitioner before the order for a device
    if the written evaluation of the beneficiary was forwarded to the treating practitioner on a date
    and the order for the device is dated an other date
    and the date is before or equal to the other date.

% Criterion 7 is the record fact "the speech language pathologist who
% evaluated B has no financial relationship with the supplier": "The SLP
% performing the beneficiary evaluation may not be an employee of or have a
% financial relationship with the supplier of the SGD."

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Accessories.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule sgd_accessory with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "Claims for accessories to SGDs must meet the general coverage requirements for the base SGD described in criteria 1-7 above":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E2512", "E2513", "E2599"]
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a speech generating device
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the speech generating device criteria for the device
    and the accessory specific criteria are met for the item.

% a mounting system: the base device's criteria suffice (a device of this model)
rule sgd_mounting_system:
the accessory specific criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E2512".

rule sgd_emg_sensor with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "Eye tracking, gaze interaction and electromyographic sensor accessories for speech generating devices are covered when furnished to individuals with a demonstrated medical need for such accessories":
the accessory specific criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E2513"
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the device is "E2510"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding tracking accessory medically needed about the beneficiary is established.

rule sgd_eye_tracking with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "Eye tracking, gaze interaction and electromyographic sensor accessories for speech generating devices are covered when furnished to individuals with a demonstrated medical need for such accessories":
the accessory specific criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E2599"
    and the accessory type of the item is ocular tracking device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding tracking accessory medically needed about the beneficiary is established.

rule sgd_alternative_input with provenance LCD L33739,
        confer "Alternative input devices are covered when a beneficiary is unable to use standard input devices":
the accessory specific criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E2599"
    and the accessory type of the item is a type
    and the type is in [alternative input device, head control mouse]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding standard input devices unusable about the beneficiary is established.

% a key guard or a power wheelchair interface: the base device's criteria
% suffice (a device of this model; the Article's coding guidelines name them
% among the separately payable accessories)
rule sgd_other_accessory:
the accessory specific criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E2599"
    and the accessory type of the item is a type
    and the type is in [protective key guard, power wheelchair interface].

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52469, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements").
rule sgd_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52469,
        confer "The medical necessity requirements for each accessory (E2599) for E2500, E2502, E2504, E2506, E2508, E2510 must be clearly documented in the formal evaluation by the SLP":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is speech_generating_devices
    and the claim is for an item
    and the accessory documentation is met for the item
    and the product identification requirement is met for the claim.

rule sgd_accessory_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52469,
        confer "For alternative input devices, there must be information in the SLP evaluation about why standard input access devices are unable to be used":
the accessory documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E2599"
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the written evaluation of the beneficiary documents the need for the item.

% any other code: a device of this model
rule sgd_no_accessory_documentation:
the accessory documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is "E2599".

rule sgd_product_identification with provenance Policy Article A52469,
        confer "When codes E2511, E2512, E2513, E2599 are billed, the claim must include all of the following information: Description of the item or service Manufacturer name Product name and number":
the product identification requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E2511", "E2512", "E2513"]
    and the claim states the product identification of the item.

rule sgd_price_list with provenance Policy Article A52469,
        confer "Additionally, claims for HCPCS code E2599 must include the supplier price list (PL) amount":
the product identification requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E2599"
    and the claim states the product identification of the item
    and the claim states the supplier price list amount of the item.

% a device of E2500-E2510: a device of this model
rule sgd_no_product_identification:
the product identification requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is in ["E2511", "E2512", "E2513", "E2599"].
